description:
Extend the existing TypeInterner one persistence boundary so it can atomically publish a canonical regular component. This is not a second Types, an alternate type language, a fact, or a compiler pass.

A type operation may use private NodeIds while it constructs one finite regular component. Before any Ty leaves the call, the interner applies the existing descriptor laws, minimizes equivalent local nodes by bisimulation, derives a canonical rooted component key, and consults the same canonical index that owns ordinary descriptors. A hit returns the already-published Ty. A miss assigns every member its final arena id and indexes every rooted member together. No reserved, redirectable, or provisional Ty may reach a descriptor, cache, fact, key, or caller.

Refactor the existing interner index rather than adding an equality authority: acyclic descriptors retain their direct structural key; cyclic members use their canonical regular-tree key. The arena remains the single Ty -> Descr authority. The temporary graph is discarded at commit return.

Renderers follow this ticket. They serialize the finalized canonical component; they must not acquire their own graph equivalence or minimization algorithm merely to make unrollings look equal.

Acceptance:
- separately constructed bisimilar self and mutual cycles return the same final Ty per root;
- every published member is complete and stable before observation;
- acyclic interning, normalization, work counters, and identity shortcuts retain their current behavior;
- the canonical census reports no duplicate regular denotation;
- no World, fact key, job, public recursive-Ty carrier, or persistent secondary graph is introduced.

It unblocks recursive rendering first. Type-changing transforms and recursive typedef resolution remain separately gated until their own cycle-safe traversal and boundary work land.
